.TH ZVM-INSTALL 1 "August 2026" "ZVM v0.9.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zvm-install \- download and install Zig and ZLS versions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zvm install
.RI [ options ]
.I version
.br
.B zvm i
.RI [ options ]
.I version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Download and install the requested Zig version.
Use
.B master
for the latest development build.
Version shorthand and aliases are accepted; see
.BR zvm (1).
.PP
By default, a new installation becomes the global default through
.IR ~/.zvm/bin .
In a shell set up with
.BR zvm-env (1),
the shell keeps its own version; run
.B zvm use
to switch it too.
Use
.B --skip-use
to install without changing the global default.
.PP
If automatic deduplication is enabled with
.BR "zvm dedupe --auto on" ,
new installations are deduplicated after installation; see
.BR zvm-dedupe (1).
.SH DOWNLOAD VERIFICATION
ZVM checks the download's SHA-256 checksum when the source supplies one.
If no checksum is available, it asks for confirmation before downloading.
Official Zig archives also require a valid Minisign signature using the
configured
.B minisignPubKey
and are checked against previously recorded hashes.
Custom version maps do not use these official-source signature checks.
ZLS archives use SHA-256 verification without Minisign signatures.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --zls
Also install a ZLS release compatible with the resolved Zig version.
.TP
.BR -f , " " --force
Install even when the version is already present.
.TP
.BR -s , " " --skip-shasum
Skip SHA-256 verification and the confirmation normally required for an
unverified download.
This weakens download verification.
Official Zig Minisign signature verification remains enabled.
.TP
.BR -k , " " --skip-use
Install Zig and any requested ZLS without changing the global default.
.TP
.BR --keep-and-rename " \fINAME\fR, " --keep " \fINAME\fR"
When a new
.B master
build replaces an installed one, keep the old build instead of deleting it.
The old build moves to a directory named after its version, such as
.IR 0.16.0-dev.1334+06d08daba ,
and
.I NAME
is saved as an alias for it; see
.BR zvm-alias (1).
Has no effect for other versions, when
.B master
is not installed, or when the installed
.B master
is already the latest build.
.TP
.BR --full
Use the full ZLS compatibility mode instead of the default runtime-only mode.
.TP
.BR --nomirror
Download Zig directly from ziglang.org instead of a community mirror.
.TP
.BR --target-os " " os
Override the target operating system.
This also sets
.B ZVM_TARGET_OS
for the operation.
.TP
.BR --target-arch " " architecture
Override the target architecture.
This also sets
.B ZVM_TARGET_ARCH
for the operation.
.TP
.BR --http.timeout " " seconds
Set the HTTP timeout for installation requests.
This also sets
.B ZVM_HTTP_TIMEOUT
for the operation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
zvm install 0.14.1
zvm i .14
zvm install --zls --full master
zvm install --keep-and-rename before-upgrade master
zvm install --target-os freebsd --target-arch x86_64 0.14.1
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zvm (1),
.BR zvm-alias (1),
.BR zvm-use (1),
.BR zvm-env (1),
.BR zvm-dedupe (1),
.BR zvm-list-remote (1),
.BR zvm-mirrorlist (1),
.BR zvm-vmu (1)
